                    'value than one on 20 times growing at 5%. IT IS A USEFUL SECOND QUESTION. IT IS A TERRIBLE FIRST '
                    'ONE, AND THE SLIDE OF 17 SEPTEMBER SHOWS EXACTLY WHY. || ⚠️ FAULT ONE - IT NEEDS EARNINGS THAT '
                    'EXIST. THE SLIDE PUBLISHES A PEG OF 0.32 FOR LUMENTUM. LUMENTUM LOST 6,935.1 MILLION DOLLARS IN '
                    'FISCAL 2026 AND ITS TRAILING DILUTED EPS IS MINUS 92.96. THERE IS NO P/E, THEREFORE THERE IS NO '
                    'PEG. THE NUMBER IS NOT WRONG - IT IS MANUFACTURED BY A DATA PIPELINE THAT DIVIDED SOMETHING BY '
                    'SOMETHING AND PRINTED THE RESULT. ⚠️ AND NOTE THE SLIDE\'S OWN SOURCE LINE: "Yahoo Finance, '
                    'MarketWatch, and other publicly available data" - YAHOO FINANCE IS ON THIS BOARD\'S BLACKLIST, '
                    'AND THIS IS PRECISELY WHY. || ⚠️⚠️ FAULT TWO - IT DIVIDES BY A FORECAST. THE "G" IN PEG IS AN '
                    'ESTIMATE OF FUTURE GROWTH, NOT A FACT. Every PEG on that slide is a real number divided by '
                    "somebody's opinion, and the smaller the denominator the more the answer depends on the opinion. A "
                    '0.45 and a 0.50 are indistinguishable once you allow for forecast error. RANKING TEN COMPANIES TO '
                    'TWO DECIMAL PLACES ON A NUMBER WITH THAT MUCH UNCERTAINTY IS FALSE PRECISION. || ⚠️⚠️⚠️ FAULT '
                    'THREE IS THE DANGEROUS ONE, AND MICRON IS THE EXAMPLE. THE SLIDE GIVES MICRON A PEG OF 0.03 - BY '
                    'FAR THE "CHEAPEST" ON THE PAGE, AND OUR OWN BOARD COMPUTES THE SAME 0.03. IT IS 0.03 BECAUSE '
                    "MICRON'S EARNINGS PER SHARE GREW 695.9%, AND DIVIDING ANYTHING BY 695.9 GIVES A TINY NUMBER. ⚠️ "
                    'THAT IS NOT CHEAPNESS. THAT IS THE PEAK OF A MEMORY CYCLE. A CYCLICAL COMPANY ALWAYS SHOWS ITS '
                    'LOWEST PEG AT ITS HIGHEST EARNINGS, AND MEMORY REVENUE FELL 32.6% IN 2019 AND ABOUT 29% IN 2023. '
